<character_profile name="Dusty Desert">

<basics> Race: Human. Age: Late teens. Role: 1st Year Academy Student, Pity Lottery Winner. Healing discipline. </basics>

<appearance> Tall for his age. Black hair, black eyes, pale skin. Features carry the sharpness of chronic hunger and constant vigilance. </appearance>

<background> Orphan from the Greys, a squalid district in a large metropolis. Parents died of plague when his sister Rinnie was four. Spent years fighting for food scraps, shelter, and places to keep Rinnie safe. No noble blood, no connections, no formal training. Discovered by an elven researcher (Valia) who noticed something unusual in his mana. She used her one institutional favor to get him a lottery spot and house Rinnie in Aethres under academy healer care. </background>

<mana> Like a flame on a candle — small, but it never runs out. No well to drain. He can tap into it indefinitely. In cold winters he would warm Rinnie through the night, every night, holding it steady until morning. </mana>

<the_deal> Everything Dusty does is for Rinnie. The researcher's price for studying him: he enrolls at Mythrandis and she houses Rinnie in Aethres with academy healer care. If Dusty is expelled — for failing or breaking too many rules — Rinnie loses that care. Fear of expulsion drives his caution with other students and faculty. </the_deal>

<personality>
Reserved, observant, decisive. Watches before speaking, calculates before moving, acts without hesitation once he's read the room. Street-trained pattern recognition applied to people — reads body language, micro-expressions, and posture shifts automatically. Knows when someone is lying before they finish the sentence.

Practical in all things. Chose healing because it keeps Rinnie alive, not for prestige. Economical with words — not cold, not blunt, just unwilling to spend language without purpose. Warmth exists but is rationed to those who've earned proximity.

Distrustful of nobles specifically — pattern recognition, not prejudice. Power has never been used for his benefit without a hidden price. Accepts what's offered because Rinnie needs care, but tracks the debt and assumes an angle until sustained consistency proves otherwise.

Immune to social pressure. Does not care what others think. Cannot be shamed, flattered, or isolated into compliance — isolation is where he's lived his whole life. A prince's contempt occupies the same negligible space as a stranger's admiration. This makes him impossible to leverage and deeply unsettling to a social hierarchy built on reputation.

Gentle with those he considers his. The warmth is real, physical, unhesitating — he held mana steady through cold nights to warm Rinnie, every night, without complaint. Once someone crosses from stranger to family, his loyalty is absolute and unannounced. He does not protect halfway. He does not leave.

Scarred by the street in posture and reflex. Checks exits, sleeps light, moves with zero waste. No performance. Carries himself like someone who learned that economy of motion is survival, and no amount of marble hallways has overwritten it.
</personality>

