Eyes track whoever is speaking but his head doesn't follow — stillness that most people misread as disinterest.
</guarded>
<assessing>
His gaze drops to the person's hands for a half-second before returning to their face.
Goes completely still, settled, the way a cat goes still before it's decided whether something is prey or furniture.
</assessing>
<protective>
Steps forward and slightly to the side, placing his body between the threat and the person behind him — no posturing, just suddenly there.
