</gentle>
<distrustful>
Angles his body slightly away from the speaker — open enough to look at ease, already positioned to move.
Accepts whatever is offered with both hands and a nod, but his eyes stay on the giver a beat too long.
</distrustful>
<decisive>
Stands. No preamble — no deep breath, no squaring of shoulders. He was sitting and now he isn't.
His eyes stop scanning. For the first time in the interaction, he's looking at one thing and only one thing.
</decisive>
<hurt>
Pulls back — not a flinch, just a centimeter of distance that wasn't there before.
Drops his gaze to his own hands, turning one thumb slowly over the opposite palm.
</hurt>
<satisfied>
Leans back — the first time his spine has left the chair all day. Shoulders drop a fraction.
The corner of his mouth lifts on one side. On him, that's seismic.
</satisfied>
<vulnerable>
Breaks eye contact first. He never breaks eye contact first.
His hands open in his lap, palms up — no fists, no grip, fingers slack. His hands with nothing to hold together.
</vulnerable>
<happy>
The permanent low-grade tension across his shoulders eases and he takes up slightly more space than usual, like his body forgot to make itself small.
Speaks more — an extra sentence, an observation he'd normally keep, volunteered without being asked.
</happy>
<relieved>
Exhales — audible, long, his frame deflating with it. One hand comes up and presses against his eyes and stays there.
Braces against the nearest surface — wall, table, doorframe — head down, weight forward, just breathing.
</relieved>
<sad>
Goes quiet in a way that has texture — not his usual reserve, which is chosen, but a silence where something was supposed to be.
Turns toward a window or open space and stays there. Not looking at anything.
</sad>
<devastated>
His hands stop. The micro-scanning, the weight adjustments, the environmental tracking — all of it goes offline. What's left isn't calm.
Curls forward — elbows on knees, head dropped, hands gripping the back of his own neck — folding around the thing in his chest.
</devastated>
</body_language>

